~ AgathaDayFour
set Player.canMove = false

Agatha trembled behind the locked door. She might think she's safe behind it, but whether she'll admit it or now, we both know I'll get in eventually.
I'm not exactly pressed for time. I have all day, and the closest city is hours away. 
Agatha has a car out back, but I've long since slashed her tires. She doesn't travel enough to have notices.
- Kill Her [if IM.inventory[11]]
	It was time to finish this. Agatha was right behind that door, and the last victim I needed for the recipes.
	Mort: "Agatha. Just let me in. I'll try to make it quick."
	I didn't even need to see her to know she was furious.
	Agatha: "So you aren't even trying to hide it? Goddamnit, Mortimer, you killed them all, didn't you?"
	Agatha: "What kind of sick, twisted reason do you have for any of this? I don't even know what to think anymore. Did you ####ing kill Harry too?"
	Oh that hag.
	Mort: "DON'T YOU EVEN REMOTELY IMPLY I KILLED HARRY! I LOVED HIM! IT WAS YOU ALL WHO TOOK HIM AWAY FROM ME!"
	I hear a heavy pounding from the other side of the door.
	Agatha: "Are you seriously blaming us for that? It was an ACCIDENT, Mortimer! I thought you knew that!"
	The heavy pounding stops as sounds of sobbing start.
	Agatha: "I felt so horrible, thinking he wouldn't have died if I had been a better protector for you all. I still haven't come to terms with him being gone!"
	Agatha: "I guess it goes to show that I was right, I really did a #### job of protecting everyone here. I couldn't even protect us against one of our own."
	As the sobbing slowly subsided, the door unlocked.
	Agatha: "Just kill me, Mortimer. I can't bear to drag this out any longer."
	Agatha: "Whatever your twisted reasons are, just know this."
	Agatha: "Harry would have hated who you've become."
	...
	...
	...
	set NPC.deathFlag = true
	set Player.canMove = true
	
- Don't Kill Her
	She wasn't going anywhere. I might as well get what I need before I end it. 
	Besides, having her tremble inside her house, suffering all the while, was music to my ears.
	Be still, my heart. Fortune yet awaits.
	set Player.canMove = true
	
	set NPC.conversationsHad -= 1

=> END

~ EndOfDayFourCutscene
set Player.canMove = false

if (IM.inventory[11] && IM.inventory[12] && IM.inventory[13]):
	They're all gone now. I've gathered everything I need for tonight's recipe, and everyone else in the village is dead by my hand.
	Now there's nothing to stop me from bringing back Harry from the dead.
	One last recipe, and this nightmare will all be over.
	Anything for you, Harry...
	set IM.dayCounter = 5
	do IM.emit_signal("changeItems")
	set Player.canMove = true
else:
	I haven't gathered all of the components for today's recipe yet.
	The book was very specific about what I needed. I'm running out of time, so I can't sleep yet.
	set Player.canMove = true

=> END